Title: _**THE GIANT**_
Credit: Written by
Author: Jack Gilmore
Description: An example screenplay, to show how scripts look on the site (and as a PDF).
Draft date: 2026-10-18
Contact: jackgilmorecreative@gmail.com

FADE IN:

EXT. MAIN STREET, BRUNSWICK - NIGHT #1#

Fog. Streetlamps make gold circles on wet pavement. The houses are white and very still.

NORA (17), headphones on, walks with her hood up. She stops.

Somewhere above the fog, something *breathes*. A slow, enormous sound, like wind through a canyon.

NORA
(pulling off headphones)
Hello?

Silence. Then a single streetlamp, high above the others, blinks.

It isn't a streetlamp. It's an _eye_.

NORA (CONT'D)
Okay. Nope.

She turns to run and walks straight into ELI (17), her neighbor, holding two coffees.

ELI
Whoa! Whoa. You look like you saw a—

NORA
Look up.

ELI
(looking up)
I don't see anything.

NORA
Exactly. Neither did I. Until it *looked back*.

ELI ^
I still don't see anything.

NORA
Keep looking.

They stare into the fog. The eye blinks again, slow and patient.

ELI
...oh.

CUT TO:

INT. NORA'S KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS #2#

The two of them sit at the table, coffees untouched. Through the window: fog, and in it, the faint outline of something far too tall.

ELI
So what do we do?

NORA
We could tell someone.

ELI
Tell them what? "There's a giant in the fog and it's very polite"?

Nora thinks about this.

NORA
(quietly)
It *was* very polite.

> THE END <

FADE OUT.
